  "reasoning": "A REST API and a GraphQL API are two different architectural styles for building web APIs. A REST API is based on a request-response model, where clients send requests to a server to retrieve or update data, whereas a GraphQL API is based on a query language, allowing clients to specify exactly what data they need and receiving only the requested data in response. GraphQL APIs are often more flexible and efficient than REST APIs, especially for complex, nested data structures or real-time updates.",
  "final_answer": "A REST API and a GraphQL API are two different architectural styles for building web APIs.",
